Crude oil is a **mixture** of hydrocarbons, mostly **alkanes** with the general formula $\ce{C_nH_{2n+2}}$. Three facts about it are marked:
it is a **finite resource** — it took millions of years to form and is being used far faster than it is replaced;
it is the **main source of hydrocarbons**;
and it is the **feedstock of the petrochemical industry**, the raw material from which plastics, medicines and detergents are made.
